.TH PAKMAN.PY 1 "2026-07-03" "2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
PakMan.py \- a robust Python package updater with batch upgrades, rollback, and logging
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python3 PakMan.py
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B PakMan.py
wraps
.B pip
to upgrade outdated Python packages. It tries a single batch upgrade first
(one resolver run), falling back to per-package upgrades with retries and
timeouts to isolate failures. Before upgrading it writes a rollback snapshot;
after upgrading it verifies the dependency graph with
.BR "pip check" .
Every run is logged to
.IR ~/.pakman.log .
.PP
If
.B uv
is installed, the outdated check uses it for a much faster query, falling
back to pip automatically on any error.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Auto-approve all upgrades without an interactive prompt.
Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-interactive .
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interactive
Show a numbered list and choose which packages to upgrade. Accepts
selections like
.BR 1,3,5\-7 ,
.BR all ,
or
.BR none .
Selection implies consent; no second confirmation prompt is shown.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-only
List outdated packages with version info and exit without upgrading.
Exits with status 3 if any outdated packages were found.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print every command that would be executed without running any of them.
Skips the confirmation prompt automatically.
.TP
.BI \-\-exclude " PKG " [ PKG " ...]"
Space-separated list of package names to skip. Matching is case-insensitive
and glob patterns are supported:
.RS
.EX
python3 PakMan.py --exclude 'boto*' setuptools
.EE
.RE
.TP
.BI \-\-only " PKG " [ PKG " ...]"
Upgrade only the listed packages. Case-insensitive, glob patterns supported.
Specifying the same name in both
.B \-\-only
and
.B \-\-exclude
is an error.
.TP
.B \-\-upgrade\-pip
Upgrade
.B pip
itself before upgrading any other packages.
.TP
.B \-\-pre
Allow installation of pre-release versions.
.TP
.B \-\-only\-binary
Pass
.B \-\-only\-binary=:all:
to pip, refusing source distributions. Installing an sdist executes its
build code; wheels do not — this flag guarantees no package code runs at
install time.
.TP
.B \-\-require\-venv
Refuse to run outside a virtual environment (exit 1). Without this flag a
prominent warning is printed instead.
.TP
.B \-\-audit
After upgrading, scan the environment for known vulnerabilities with
.BR pip-audit .
Skipped with a hint if pip-audit is not installed.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-uv
Use pip for the outdated check even if
.B uv
is installed.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-rollback
Skip writing the rollback snapshot file.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-batch
Skip the batch upgrade attempt and go straight to per-package upgrades.
.TP
.BI \-\-export " FILE"
After all upgrades complete, run
.B pip freeze
and write the output to
.IR FILE .
If the freeze command fails, a warning is printed and no file is written.
.TP
.B \-\-notify
Send a native macOS notification (via
.BR osascript )
when the run completes. Notification text is escaped to prevent AppleScript
injection.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the outdated package list as a JSON array and exit. No upgrades are
performed.
.TP
.B \-\-log\-json
Append one structured JSON record per run (upgraded packages, failures,
dependency conflicts, elapsed time, exit code) to
.IR ~/.pakman_history.jsonl .
.TP
.BI \-\-retries " N"
Number of retry attempts per package on the fallback path. Default is
.BR 2 ,
minimum is
.BR 1 .
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " SECS"
Timeout per package in seconds; the batch attempt gets timeout multiplied by
the package count. Default is
.BR 600 .
A package stuck building from source becomes a recorded failure instead of
hanging the run.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success — nothing to do, or all upgrades succeeded.
.TP
.B 1
Fatal error (non-TTY without \-y, \-\-require\-venv outside a venv, ...).
.TP
.B 2
Run completed but one or more packages failed.
.TP
.B 3
.B \-\-check\-only
found outdated packages.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted with Ctrl-C.
.SH FEATURES
.SS Batch Upgrade with Per-Package Fallback
All packages are first upgraded in a single
.B pip install --upgrade
call — one resolver run instead of N. Only if the batch fails does PakMan
fall back to per-package upgrades (with parallel wheel prefetch) to isolate
the failure. Note that a batch resolver run may choose a version other than
the newest if a newer version conflicts with another package's requirements;
the post-run
.B pip check
covers this.
.SS Rollback Snapshot
Before upgrading, current versions are written as
.I pkg==version
lines to
.IR ~/.pakman_rollback_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.txt .
Undo an entire run with:
.RS
.EX
pip install -r ~/.pakman_rollback_<timestamp>.txt
.EE
.RE
The five newest snapshots are kept; older ones are pruned.
.SS Dependency Health Check
.B pip check
runs automatically after every upgrade and surfaces broken dependency graphs
in the output, the log, and the JSON history.
.SS Security Hardening
Package names are validated against PEP 508 naming rules before reaching any
subprocess. The log file is created with mode 0600. Every pip invocation
writes an AUDIT line with the exact command and exit code. Pip's own version
self-check is disabled on every call.
.SS Clean Interrupts and Cron Safety
Ctrl-C mid-upgrade prints how many packages were upgraded, failed, and not
attempted, then exits 130. In a non-TTY session without
.BR \-y ,
the tool exits 1 immediately instead of hanging on the prompt.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Standard interactive upgrade:
.EX
python3 PakMan.py
.EE
.TP
Pick packages from a numbered list:
.EX
python3 PakMan.py -i
.EE
.TP
Auto-approve, skip all boto packages, notify:
.EX
python3 PakMan.py -y --exclude 'boto*' --notify
.EE
.TP
Wheels only — never execute sdist build code:
.EX
python3 PakMan.py --only-binary -y
.EE
.TP
Refuse to touch global site-packages:
.EX
python3 PakMan.py --require-venv -y
.EE
.TP
Upgrade, then scan for known vulnerabilities:
.EX
python3 PakMan.py -y --audit
.EE
.TP
Upgrade pip first, then everything, export freeze when done:
.EX
python3 PakMan.py --upgrade-pip -y --export requirements.txt
.EE
.TP
Cron-friendly run with JSON history:
.EX
python3 PakMan.py -y --log-json --no-rollback
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.pakman.log
Timestamped log of all runs with per-command AUDIT lines. Mode 0600.
.TP
.I ~/.pakman_history.jsonl
One JSON record per run when
.B \-\-log\-json
is set. Mode 0600.
.TP
.I ~/.pakman_rollback_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.txt
Pre-upgrade version snapshots; the five newest are kept.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Python 3.10 or later.
.B pip
must be available for the active interpreter
.RB ( "python \-m pip" ).
.PP
The
.B \-\-notify
flag requires
.B osascript
(available by default on macOS).
.PP
Optional:
.B uv
for fast outdated checks,
.B pip-audit
for
.BR \-\-audit .
.SH AUTHOR
Anirban Bagchi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pip (1),
.BR python3 (1)
